module gunbc.floor_discovery_scaffold



data floor_discovery_hand_rust_scaffold: std.disposition.Disposition = std.disposition.Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: std.disposition.SingleAuthority,
  bind: std.decl_ref.DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_discovery_producer",
    decl_name: "discover_floor_corpus_rows_from_host_facts",
    field: std.decl_ref.WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data floor_discovery_dissolve_trigger: std.dissolution.DissolutionCondition = std.dissolution.unbound_dissolution(description: "🟡 dissolve-on: floor_discovery_hand_rust_bridge — floor_discovery_producer.dag is roster authority; Rust host still realizes effect-reach reclassification (apply_effect_reach_derived_reads_live_tree), parallel tree walks for build_floor_lens_import_graph, and invoke_floor_discovery_producer interpreter transport via discover_floor_witness_roster; DISSOLVES WHEN discovery admission consumes v2.lens.effect_reach directly and lens-graph feed the .dag producer closure (witness: dag/test/claim/floor_discovery_hand_rust_equivalence_witness_test.dag). Legacy discover_floor_corpus_rows_inner_rust_legacy deleted; discover_floor_corpus_rows / check_floor_filename_hygiene / _inner / _scoped arms deleted. Transport surface enumerated for this receipt (review 44710): invoke_floor_discovery_producer delegates to invoke_floor_discovery_producer_over_corpus(producer_roots, corpus_roots, ...), which de-fuses the two roles the single source_roots list carried — producer_roots locates the MACHINERY (this module's producer entry), corpus_roots is the SUBJECT walked and judged. Production passes one list for both, so the split is role-naming with no behaviour change, and it dissolves with the transport it parameterizes. The producer entry is a typed WorkspaceRootRelativeEntry value resolved through cli_run.rs resolve_workspace_entry, which anchors it against process_workspace_root before the shared resolver observes it. The filename-hygiene entry was the second such value until gunbc#8155 deleted the `__`-basename rule it resolved for; that rule guarded a zero-row population, and reaching it cost a whole-corpus path walk plus this separate entry resolve on every discovery-bearing run.")

data floor_entry_resolution_host_boundary_note: String = "ENTRY-ANCHOR host boundary: cli_run.rs WorkspaceRootRelativeEntry names the family intent and resolve_workspace_entry is its single host realization. FLOOR_DISCOVERY_PRODUCER_ENTRY flows through it; no per-target anchor helper or manually maintained hand-Rust count remains. FLOOR_NAMING_HYGIENE_ENTRY was the second such entry until gunbc#8155 deleted the `__`-basename rule it existed to resolve — that rule guarded a population of zero with no stated rationale, and reaching it cost a whole-corpus path walk plus a separate entry resolve on every discovery-bearing run. GUARANTEE RUNG: documentary brand plus one anchoring site, not a construction wall — WorkspaceRootRelativeEntry remains directly constructible inside cli_run.rs, so the type alone does not make an absolute or otherwise invalid entry unwritable. NEXT TRIGGER: move the type behind a separate-module opaque constructor that accepts only validated workspace-root-relative paths. DISSOLVE-ON DEBT REMAINING: this change satisfies the typed-entry half of the former trigger but resolve_workspace_entry still joins against process_workspace_root in hand Rust; the hand-Rust anchor dissolves only when the shared resolver or a modeled host realization owns workspace-relative entry semantics. Concrete ROADMAP row: gunbc.roadmap_authority v1-hand-queue-drain (Work through the remaining hand-written files the products need)."

data floor_entry_resolution_host_boundary_discriminator: String = "resolve_workspace_entry"

data floor_discovery_producer_entry: String = "src/v2/workflow/floor_discovery_producer.dag"

data floor_discovery_equivalence_test_sidecar_misplaced: String = "misplaced_wire_contract_decl_drives_discover_to_err"

data floor_discovery_equivalence_test_scan_wire_contract: String = "scan_detects_coproduct_wire_contract_data"

data floor_discovery_equivalence_test_narrowed_corpus_control: String = "clean_dag_file_leaves_narrowed_discovery_ok"

data floor_discovery_scope_semantics_note: String = "discovery_scope_dirs semantics (intentional, review 41826): the producer walk (floor_discovery_walk_dir over all source_roots) applies tree-wide hygiene — filename __ refusal, test-marked-decl sidecar, wire-contract sidecar — before finalize. discover_floor_witness_roster applies discovery_scope_dirs only as a post-walk row filter (cli_run.rs apply_discovery_scope_dirs_filter), not as a pre-walk skip. Legacy build_floor_lens_hygiene_graph short-circuited sidecar checks outside scope; the new shape refuses on any hygiene violation anywhere under source_roots even when witness enrollment is scoped. Today ci_floor_plan discovery_scope_dirs is always [] so production CI is unchanged; non-empty scope is for narrowed roster projection only, not narrowed hygiene."
